{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_100","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed the full research pass and wrote the deliverables.\n\nThe main result is that `gpt-4.1` behaves like a structured but biased simulator, not a true superset simulator. Persona conditioning improved Social IQA accuracy from `0.744` to `0.789` and increased ultimatum policy diversity from `2` to `5` distinct policies, but all conditions still accepted unfair offers too easily, which points to rationality/compliance bias and weak tail coverage.\n\nKey files:\n- [REPORT.md](/workspaces/theory-of-simulation-6163-codex/REPORT.md:1)\n- [planning.md](/workspaces/theory-of-simulation-6163-codex/planning.md:1)\n- [src/run_experiments.py](/workspaces/theory-of-simulation-6163-codex/src/run_experiments.py:1)\n- [src/analyze_results.py](/workspaces/theory-of-simulation-6163-codex/src/analyze_results.py:1)\n- [README.md](/workspaces/theory-of-simulation-6163-codex/README.md:1)\n\nArtifacts generated:\n- `results/raw/social_iqa_gpt-4.1.jsonl`\n- `results/raw/ultimatum_gpt-4.1.jsonl`\n- `results/summary/summary_gpt-4.1.csv`\n- `results/summary/analysis_gpt-4.1.json`\n- `figures/social_iqa_distribution_gpt-4.1.png`\n- `figures/ultimatum_curves_gpt-4.1.png`\n\nValidation completed:\n- Environment isolation used via the existing `.venv`\n- Full real-model run executed on `2026-05-05`\n- Output counts verified: `270` Social IQA rows, `405` ultimatum rows\n- Report and figures present\n\nMain limitation: the local `OpinionQA` mirror did not include the full human-response tables, so the strongest subgroup-distribution test had to be deferred and is documented in the report."}}
